{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>This do: take you censers.</b> What reason did he have to say this to them? He said to them: Among the nations there are many rites and many priests, and all of them do not gather in one house; but we have only one HaShem, one Ark, one Torah, one altar, and one High Priest — yet you, 250 men, each one seeking the High Priesthood! I too desire that. Here for you is the most beloved service of all — it is the incense, most beloved of all the offerings, and the deadly poison is placed within it, for through it Nadav and Avihu were burned. Therefore he warned them: <b>and the man whom HaShem shall choose, he is the holy one</b> — he is already in his holiness. But do we not know that whoever He chooses is the holy one? Rather, Moses said to them: I say to you, so that you not incur guilt — the one whom He chooses will emerge alive, and all of you will perish (Tanchuma)." "<b>Censers.</b> Vessels in which one scoops embers, and they have a handle."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:14.662890942Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}